Both repos' bridge documents name work that was deferred or flagged when the
integration landed. None of it needed LogPup running, so none of it needed to
wait.

1. safeNext refused '//' but not a leading backslash. Browsers normalise '\' to
   '/' in URLs, so '/\evil.example' passes a '//' check and then behaves as a
   protocol-relative URL — an open redirect on a sign-in route. LogPup's doc
   flagged the minter's copy; in fact BOTH copies were missing the rule, and the
   receiver (src/app/sso/logpup/page.tsx) is the end that performs the redirect.
   The two private copies are now one tested src/lib/safeNext.ts, matching
   LogPup's src/lib/safe-next.ts rule for rule, with the differing fallback
   ('/' vs '/dashboard') passed in by the caller.

2. Nothing pruned logpup_sso_redemptions. The sweep is now a step inside the
   existing cron/maintenance-lifecycle job rather than a new cron, as
   LOGPUP_TASKS_INTEGRATION.md asked. One 500-doc batch per run, expires_at <=
   now, and it swallows its own errors so it can never fail the maintenance
   announcements the endpoint is polled for.

3. logpupApi's fallback base URL pointed at logpup.altavision.lk. LogPup is
   deployed at management.altavision.lk, so a dropped LOGPUP_APP_URL would have
   degraded the tasks section to "empty" instead of "misconfigured". The API key
   is also trimmed now: a .env parser strips surrounding whitespace and a
   hosting dashboard does not, and LogPup's bridgeKeyValid compares digests with
   no trim of its own — so the same value can work locally and 401 in
   production.

Verification is partial and the limit is the environment, not the change: the
npm registry is unreachable from here, so node_modules could not be installed
and neither `npm test` nor `npx next build --webpack` could run. What did run:
src/lib/safeNext.ts type-checks clean standalone under --strict, its 6 tests
compile and pass under node --test (6 pass, 0 fail), and all four edited files
are free of syntax errors. The full three-command ladder still has to be run
where the dependencies resolve.

